# Radius: one base, role rungs, geometry exceptions

`--radius` is the only consumer override. Chrome, Card, and Dialog **all respond to it**. They do not share one class.

| Role | Class | Why |
|------|-------|-----|
| Chrome | `rounded-md` | Button, Input, ButtonGroup, Tabs — sits on a panel (`--radius − 2px`) |
| Panels | `rounded-lg` | Card, Alert, popover — **is** `--radius` |
| Overlays | `rounded-xl` | Dialog, Sheet, Drawer — outer must be larger than padded inner content |

Do not flatten Card/Dialog to `rounded-md` to match ButtonGroup. The step is concentric nesting, not three brands.

## Stay separate (do not “unify”)

- **Circles** → `rounded-full`: radio disc, Switch + thumb, Slider thumb, Avatar, scrollbar thumb, drawer handle, status dots
- **Compact chips** (short side ≤ 20px) → `rounded-xs`: Badge, kbd, Combobox chip, 20px icon buttons. `rounded-md` on `h-5` is a stadium at Soft.
- **Thin tracks** → stadium is correct: Progress / Slider bar

Never `rounded-full` on Badge/Button/Tabs. Never `rounded-md` on Switch/Avatar/radio disc. Never hardcode `border-radius: Npx`.

Nested chip-in-shell: `inner = outer − inset` (Tabs / sliding Radio already do this).
